{"summary": "The proposed revisions address critical race conditions and memory leaks in the artwork transition system, but fail to specify how the reducer must change to prevent visual flickering during the 'settle' phase.",
"verdict": "REVISE",
"items": [{"issue": "The proposal to nullify the base layer in the reducer may cause a visual 'pop' or flash if the incoming layer's opacity isn't fully 1.0 before the base is removed.", "evidence": "src/art/ArtBackdrop.tsx: The transition logic relies on a 2400ms timeout to 'settle', but there is no evidence of a CSS transition duration that guarantees synchronization.", "change": "Specify that the reducer must only nullify the base layer after a delay that exceeds the CSS crossfade duration, or implement a 'completed' state in the reducer.", "check": "Verify that the transition from incoming to base is seamless without a flicker when the base layer is purged from the DOM."}, {"issue": "The fix for auto-advance double-skips is insufficient as it only resets the interval, not the internal state of the timer logic.", "evidence": "src/art/ArtViewer.tsx: The setInterval uses a closure over 'previous' and 'elapsed.current' which may persist across re-renders if not handled carefully.", "change": "Ensure the auto-advance useEffect explicitly clears the previous interval and resets the 'previous' timestamp to Date.now() upon every 'selected.id' change.", "check": "Verify that manual navigation resets the 60-second countdown exactly to 0ms without inheriting elapsed time from the previous artwork."}, {"issue": "Lack of validation for 'failed' state handling during automated playback.", "evidence": "src/art/ArtViewer.tsx: The auto-advance interval checks 'if (failed) return', which will permanently stall the 'Play collection' sequence if a single image fails to load.", "change": "Implement a timeout or retry limit within the auto-advance logic to automatically skip to the next artwork if the current one remains in a 'failed' state for more than 5 seconds.", "check": "Simulate a 404 on an image during 'Play collection' and verify the sequence continues to the next artwork automatically."}]}
